module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.hand_shim_shadows_an_emitted_module

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data hand_shim_shadows_an_emitted_module: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "hand_shim_shadows_an_emitted_module" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a hand-authored Rust copy of a .dag module is substituted for the emitted one, and when the emitter evolves the copy silently stops matching both the emitter and the authority** (INVALID STATE: tools.self_host_module_behavioral_transport_roster rows overwrote emitted modules with hand shims -- a shared std-bridge directory (v2_std_node, v2_std_algebra, v2_std_collection, v2_std_diagnostic, v2_std_integer) plus per-row shim lib.rs files -- so the self-host behavioral receipts linked a crate that was neither the emitter's output nor the .dag's meaning. HARM, THREE MEASURED FACES: (1) self_host_03_normalize_behavioral_receipt_holds was red for 13 E0308 because the v2_std_diagnostic shim, last touched in #10929, still spelled Diagnostics as `enum Diagnostics` with `rejected_with_pending(pending: Rc<Diagnostics>, ..)` after the emitter moved the None | Some coproduct to Option<Rc<NonEmptyDiagnostics>>; the red was read as an EMITTER defect (value/Rc boundary at call sites) and briefed as one, while the emitted crate alone cargo-checked clean. (2) The lax v2_std_node shim kept a MALFORMED fixture green: the body_producer driver's Transform body carried zero edges, which v2.std.node behavior_edges_conform refuses (Transform needs count(children) >= 1); against the emitted module the fixture is refused. (3) The same slice hid a hollow ORACLE: the seed's hand-retained v1_compiler::v2_compiler_normalize answered well_formed = true for every tree, and the old fault input (an empty Disj) is accepted by both realizations, so the 03_normalize fault arm was red whichever way emitted normalize behaved -- parity with a stub that accepts everything is not evidence. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the shim is a SECOND realization of a module whose authority is a .dag file, so it is the section 3 fork at the realization layer; nothing ties its bytes to the emitter, so it drifts on every emitter change that touches the module's shape, and it fails in whichever direction the drift points -- toward a compile red that blames the emitter, or toward a laxer check that greens a wrong input. The dissolution trigger the bridge carried ('v2 std self-emits and gunbc emits seed-linked extern imports without hand ABI bridges') had already fired and nothing read it. RECOGNITION RULE: when a witness builds 'the emitted X', read the assembly and ask which bytes of X the emitter actually produced; any file written from the repository over an emitted path is a hand realization and is presumed stale. When a behavioral receipt compares against a hand oracle, run one input the authority REFUSES through both sides before trusting parity. RUNG FOUND AT: silent -- the receipts are outside the required lane, so the red sat on main unnoticed. RUNG NOW, FOR THE ROSTER: structurally impossible -- every shim row was censused (emitted closure builds and the driver passes with no shim), the shims were deleted, and ModuleBehavioralTransportConfig / cssl_seed_linked_behavioral_receipt no longer carry shim_lib_rel or shim_writes, so a row cannot name a shim. CEILING AND RESIDUE: the class survived one layer down, in the seed's other hand-retained oracles the receipts compared against, each a hand realization that could be laxer than its authority exactly as v2_compiler_normalize was. #12316 deleted seven (resolve, infer, program_assembly, source_authority, program_partition, target_carriers, discovery_enumeration); the last five (body_producer, parse_engine_hooks, use_site_verdict, compile, tokenize) were deleted with the usv_pilot_v2_std_algebra, usv_pilot_v2_std_collection and usv_pilot_v2_std_node scaffolds that existed only to back two of them, and every self_host behavioral driver now checks its .dag contract on the emitted module with no v1_compiler import, so no receipt's expected value comes from a hand copy of the module under test. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the behavioral oracle is the v1 interpreter's evaluation of the SAME .dag entry rather than a hand-retained Rust module, sufficient that no receipt's expected value can come from a copy of the module under test. Replacing one stub with a better stub does not discharge it.)",
    "**RECURRENCE ONE LAYER OUT: THE WITNESS DRIVERS** (2026-10-03). The shims were deleted and the rows' hand-written Rust DRIVERS were left: fifteen witness_main.rs files restating each subject's .dag contract against the EMITTED spelling of v2.std.node. Nothing compiles them except the fleet-dispatched behavioral instrument, so they sit outside every per-change compiled population. RECEIPT: gunbc#12799 cut EdgeLabel root-first and touched none of the fifteen; fleet run 37092365386 then failed to build three of them -- 07_target_carriers and program_partition on E0599 for the deleted EdgeLabel::Named, 04_infer on E0308 passing Rc<Node> where infer takes Rc<ResolvedTree>. The failures had been invisible behind the libc E0433 of probe_manifest_overwrites_emitted_dependency_demand, so the rows read as one defect while carrying two. REPAIR FOR THOSE THREE ROWS: the contract is a .dag function (inject_fault: Bool) -> Bool in a claim module whose closure contains the subject (v2.test.claim.self_host_contract.*), typechecked on the floor against the real declarations, emitted into the same crate as its subject, and called by a driver RENDERED from the roster row (tools.self_host_curated_seed_linked_harness CsslWitnessDriver EmittedContractDriver, cssl_contract_driver_main_source). The receipt also runs the same contract interpreted, so a row holds only when the emitted and interpreted realizations agree. The three hand files are deleted with the migration. RESIDUE, COUNTED: twelve rows still carry HandDriverFile and can drift the same way; the arm takes no new rows and each remaining row migrates by deleting its file.)",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "tools.self_host_curated_seed_linked_harness", decl_name: "cssl_seed_linked_behavioral_receipt", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "tools.self_host_module_behavioral_transport_roster", decl_name: "ModuleBehavioralTransportConfig", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
